By using the keyboard. 

Hold shift and use the arrow keys to highlight text.

Copy is control+c
Paste is control+v
Cut is control+x

Find is control+f

Undo is control+z
Redo is control+y

If you want to see them all (there's so many) you can press control+e (this lets you use commands within the text editor, which you will see on the bottom) and type "help defaultkeys". You can just scroll down and  see the list. Press control+g to close it.

If you'd like to turn on or off the spell checker, you can press control+e and type "set aspell.check (on/off)". You're able to adjust the quality of the suggestions by using "set aspell.sugmode (ultra, fast, normal, slow)." You can also move your cursor to the underlines word and open the control+e menu and type "acceptsug" to correct the word, you can press tab after to cycle through different suggestions. You can also type "addpersonal" If you want to save that special word.

