When you're on your homepage and decide to make a new file, you'll notice it asks if you want an empty,r MLA format, or smart file. empty is empty and MLA format is pretty interesting. If you choose MLA format, it'll make a file ending in ".txt". When you open it it'll look like an interesting format, but just fill it out normally. Put your full name, instructor name, yadayada. It's simple to use, just keep the formatting the same, the spaces between each line are essential so make sure they stay. You can make as many body paragraphs as you want just make sure to put a space between them. When you're done, exit the file and while its high-lighted, press 'c' and it'll make a duplicate of that file that ends in ".docx". You wont be able to open those files on this device. Next, we have the "smart" file. This one is meant to be for quickly jotting down notes, or making lists. The template should be explanatory but if its not i'll explain it for you. The numbers symbolize a section and only one section with each number can exist. If you try and create a "1. " section when it already exists, it will rename the existing section instead. Next, you can create bullets using characters. 
For Example:
1. First section
1a. First sections first bullet
1b. first sections second bullet

The bullets are sorted by alphabetical order. You can exit and come back to the document at any moment and continue to update it by using the same format. You may also write plain text anywhere in the document and it will be transported to the top of the document when you return.

That's the basics, you should be able to figure out the rest. Good luck

